  <learnings>["Ruling the test suite inadmissible as evidence is what made this audit productive. Four prior reviews accepted 'tests pass'; once auditors were required to demonstrate breaks in a scratch fabric, six critical findings surfaced in one pass — including two that had been latent through every earlier review.", "The live repo being unmigrated is not a configuration detail, it is a safety posture: it disengages the working CAS, leaves 11 of 64 strands CAS-blind, and means every v3 structural protection covers zero of the founder's data. Check which epoch the DATA is in before crediting a fix that lives in a later epoch.", "A documented invariant with no checker is worse than an undocumented one — it reads as a guarantee. strand.ts:140 documents 'parentStateId (always the ledger tip)' and nothing anywhere compares it, which is exactly how a detected crash-break launders itself into a permanent 'all intact'.", "Detection without repair is a dead end a real crash will find. Warpline detects nearly everything and repairs nothing: a torn tail line — reachable by plain disk-full, no crash required — bricks every verb including fabric verify itself, and the documented recovery is a text editor.", "Guards that exist but are bypassed are a distinct and common defect class here: restore.ts has the correct dirty-dest policy and two call sites skip it; the stake journal that would make truncation loud is already written to disk and verify never reads it. Look for the correct implementation before writing a new one.", "'Fails open' and 'fails open AND reports success' deserve separate lists. The second class — a merge that drops a file and seals CLEAN, a shadow refusal that returns isError:false — is what actually loses data, and it is invisible to anyone reading exit codes."]</learnings>
